ment_prompt/which-choice-is-a-complete-sentence-f55d6f72c6.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/bite-3784fdd141.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/date-75868fc17d.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/deep-e3054d47be.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/food-fa579b9bf4.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/guide-503c0aee20.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/hide-58f49e39cf.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/hope-fc69325f16.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/lake-ce59b3a1ec.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/light-9f1ceef2a6.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/like-d520d1d2e5.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/line-27915b1e33.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/made-2a7d35e2fe.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/make-c18a8deb9e.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/meat-cb2e88bc60.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/name-9a748e92a5.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/nine-200651a3c9.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/pack-09bd7b3f4d.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/race-8c72965213.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/rain-77e7f4fa6e.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/road-0981a71559.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/rope-5adf472794.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/seat-a14e91a6a5.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/seed-325cb69d42.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/side-3d48670f2b.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/snake-e24026d113.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/soon-839140e2d6.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/soup-1b5cde969c.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/stone-486b4691a2.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/street-31037957ab.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/take-48a0e9f377.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/tune-a29852eea1.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/twice-f98cd934e6.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/week-5626b52555.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/wide-06aafe8dc2.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/pine-685d8d98cd.mp3","A hat was necessary for a child to join the walk.","A pupil without a signed form could take a book.","A signed form was required, but it did not mean a pupil took a book.","A star was needed for a box to be sent, but not every starred box went.","All the new books were below the top shelf.","All trays other than the green one had two cups.","Anya pulled one handle on a carrying box to check it. When she lifted both handles, the unchecked handle came loose. After repairing it, she tested each handle separately before carrying the box.","Anyone in the show wearing a blue ribbon was a dancer, not a singer.","Apples were in all the baskets; pears were in just one.","Arun crowded the drying rack with wet paintings touching edge to edge. Two pictures stuck together. He moved the next paintings onto separate spaces with gaps between them. They dried without sticking.","Aya packed a painted clay tile while its surface was still wet. The wrapping stuck to the picture. She painted a new tile and left it on the rack until it was dry before wrapping it.","Ben rebuilt the top of his block tower whenever it leaned. It kept leaning because a folded cloth was under one corner of the base. He flattened the cloth and rebuilt the base. The tower stayed upright.","Bo put the brushes away before washing them.","Bo washed the brushes while they remained in the cupboard.","Both bags held towels.","Both bags were without towels.","Boxes without stars were the only ones sent.","Check that a block base is firm and level.","Check that the pages show the whole walking route.","Children could enter whenever they reached the closed gate.","Children entered before the adult opened the gate.","Children wearing hats had to stay at school.","Choose a blanket large enough for the visitors.","Choose a box that is easy to carry.","Choose a bus color that passengers can recognize.","Choose a map large enough for the group to share.","Choose a picnic place with room for everyone.","Choose a puzzle with enough pieces for everyone.","Choose card colors that stand out against the wall.","Choose clear pictures of the objects to collect.","Choose colors that make a toy cart easy to find.","Choose colors that make the model’s shape easy to see.","Choose fabric that will move freely in the wind.","Choose flag colors that visitors can see clearly.","Choose paint colors that show against the background.","Choose plant labels that can survive getting wet.","Choose plants that fit the space on a shelf.","Choose scissors suited to the thickness of the paper.","Choose scissors that can cut the paper strips cleanly.","Choose strong paper for a pocket that holds books.","Choose teams with equal numbers of players.","Choose wrapping that is large enough for the box.","Cleo changed the only written plan for her puppet scene and later forgot the earlier ending. Before her next change, she copied the plan onto another sheet. She could compare both endings and choose one.","Count the seedlings before carrying a full tray.","Dad put out the candles before the song ended.","Dan rebuilt a small bridge from a drawing and began putting the drawing away. He looked back at it and noticed a support he had left out. He added that support before trying the bridge.","Dani set out a high stool for the visiting drummer without asking what she needed. The drummer’s feet could not reach her pedal. Dani asked about the drum, then brought a low seat. The drummer could use the pedal.","Dev called out the drum rhythm once and expected the group to remember it. They stopped at different places. He drew a row of beat marks and pointed along them. The group could follow the same rhythm.","Esme stuffed every costume into one small bag. The zipper could not close. She moved some costumes into a second bag. Both bags closed, and the costumes stayed inside on the walk to the hall.","Every child had finished the puzzle.","Every child joined, whether or not they wore a hat.","Every child planted at least three seeds.","Every child planted exactly two seeds.","Every flag was left unpainted.","Every large crate contained books.","Every pupil with a signed form took a book.","Every round and square button was used.","Every round button was used, and every square button was left unused.","Every seat beside the door was taken.","Every shelf received some new books.","Every singer wore the same ribbon as the dancers.","Every starred box was sent to the hall.","Every tray had two cups.","Every used button was square.","Felix tied a large bow across the mouth of his cardboard trumpet. Almost no sound came out. He moved the bow onto the side, leaving the opening clear. He could hear the trumpet again.","Give both teams a chance to practice first.","Give each builder a share of the available blocks.","Give every player a chance to lead the music.","Give the cart a handle that is comfortable to hold.","Hana kept adding soap to the wash bowl after the water was already bubbly. Foam spilled over the edge. For the next bowl she added a small amount and stopped when it was enough to wash the tools.","Hang a wet coat where it can dry.","Hugo pulled both ends of a knotted ribbon to free it. The knot grew tighter. He loosened one small loop with his fingers instead. The ribbon came free without another hard pull.","Ivy carried a seed packet to the bean bed because its picture looked like beans. The gardener showed her that it was a pea packet. Ivy read the names on the remaining packets before taking the bean seeds.","Jin explained the model while holding its opening toward himself. His partner could not see the part he named. Jin moved around to his partner’s side and turned the model. The opening was now visible to both of them.","Keep a finished painting safe from dusty shelves.","Keep a list of people who borrow the stamp set.","Keep a note of who has borrowed each tray.","Keep a record of how many beads you collect.","Keep cleaning cloths away from the toy collection.","Keep coats low enough for children to reach.","Keep cut paper strips together until the craft begins.","Keep different paint colors in their own pots.","Keep loose card pieces in a labelled storage tray.","Keep the path beside a busy door clear.","Kofi chose a beautiful basket with very wide gaps to carry small counters. Counters fell through. He tried a plain tub with solid sides. The counters stayed inside, so he carried them in the tub.","Lanterns on both tables were lit.","Leave enough space inside a bus for its seats.","Lena used a thick brush to paint the tiny windows on her model. Paint covered the wall around each window. She changed to a thin brush and painted the remaining windows without covering the walls.","Leo mixed a batch of plaster before making a space for the mold. While he searched for a clear tray, the mixture became too stiff to pour. For the next batch he set out the mold and tray before mixing.","Listen to other players before choosing an instrument.","Match a gift to the interests of its owner.","Mateo lent out the class puppets without writing down the borrowers. At tidy-up he did not know who still had one. Next time he wrote each name beside a puppet picture and ticked it when the puppet returned.","Max changed the class shop’s opening time on his own note. The helpers arrived at the old time. Before changing it again, he spoke to each helper and changed the shared sign. They arrived together.","Measure a cupboard before choosing what to store.","Measure the model before deciding where to display it.","Mei looked for a book by jumping between several shelves. She kept returning to shelves she had already searched. She began at one end and checked each shelf in turn. On the next shelf she found the book.","Mila left her paper shop signs outside when rain began. The words ran down the paper. She made new signs and put them beneath the stall’s clear roof. Rain fell around the stall, but the signs stayed dry.","Nia was asked to put the seed tray in a bright place. She chose the sunny outdoor wall, where the rain flooded it. She checked with the gardener and moved it to the bright indoor window the gardener had meant.","No child had finished the puzzle.","No dancer wore a blue ribbon.","No tickets remained for sale when the doors opened.","Noor finished after Tess but before Sol.","Noor finished after both Tess and Sol.","Noor finished before both Tess and Sol.","One bag held all the towels.","Only one basket contained any fruit.","Only the green tray had two cups.","Only the lanterns on the left table were lit.","Only the lanterns on the right table were lit.","Only the yellow flag was left unpainted.","Only the yellow flag was painted.","Only two children planted seeds.","Owen filled a whole watering can from an old jug. Water leaked through a crack and soaked the bench. He poured a little water into the next jug first. That jug stayed dry underneath, so he used it.","Pears were in all the baskets; apples were in just one.","Pia copied that the model needed three strips, but left out their length. Her group cut strips too short for the roof. She checked the plan and wrote both the number and the length. The new strips reached across.","Plan what a basket will hold before decorating.","Rabbit feeding happened after both lunch and music.","Rabbit feeding happened before both lunch and music.","Rabbit feeding happened between lunch and music.","Rosa never watered the pot, even after it dried.","Rosa tried to copy a large map in one hurried drawing. Several streets were missing. She copied one small square of the map at a time, checking each square before moving on. Her new drawing included the streets.","Rosa waited for dry soil before watering.","Rosa watered while the soil was still wet.","Sam started building the puppet stage before checking its fasteners. He held two walls up for a long time while a friend searched for clips. Next time he collected the clips and walls together before joining the stage.","Send a picnic invitation in a strong envelope.","Share the watering jobs between the gardeners.","Some children had not finished the puzzle.","Some large crates held books, and no small crate held books.","Some new books went on the top shelf.","Some small crates contained books.","Some tickets remained for sale when the doors opened.","Sort differently colored beads into separate groups.","Sort puzzle pieces into groups with similar colors.","Sort the beans by size before comparing them.","Store stamps where damp air cannot reach them.","Take a bag that keeps picnic food together.","The adult had to open the gate before children entered.","The brushes were already washed when Bo put them away.","The candles were out before the song began.","The free seats described were beside the door, not the window.","The last clap came after both movements.","The last clap came before both movements.","The last clap came between standing up and sitting down.","The library opened before the repair.","The library stayed closed after the repair was finished.","The players remained inside throughout the afternoon.","The players went outside before it began to rain.","The players went outside while the rain continued.","The repair came before the library opened.","The song had already ended when Dad put out the candles.","Theo pulled the ribbons out of a woven mat and forgot their order. Before repairing another section, he drew where each ribbon went. He followed the drawing and put the ribbons back in the same places.","Tickets first went on sale after the doors opened.","Two seats beside the window were free.","Use a handle large enough for your hand.","Use a straight pole to display the finished flag.","Use sturdy paper for a list that stays up.","We waited until the gate opened.","Which choice is a complete sentence?","While I held the ladder, Dad climbed up.","Write a pattern title that describes its finished shape.","Write the owner’s name clearly on the book pocket.","Yusuf counted how long two toy cars rolled, but started counting at different moments. His numbers did not compare the full journeys. He rolled them again and began counting at the start line each time.","ada hung the picture list above her own head. the younger children could not see what to collect. she crouched beside them, noticed the shelf in their way, and moved the list down where they could see it. jin explained the model while holding its opening toward himself. his partner could not see the part he named. jin moved around to his partner’s side and turned the model. the opening was now visible to both of them.","ada hung the picture list above her own head. the younger children could not see what to collect. she crouched beside them, noticed the shelf in their way, and moved the list down where they could see it.","alma poured paint onto a mixing plate and then went to find a brush and water. the paint dried while she searched. before her next painting she put the brush, water and plate together, then poured the paint. sam started building the puppet stage before checking its fasteners. he held two walls up for a long time while a friend searched for clips. next time he collected the clips and walls together before joining the stage.","alma poured paint onto a mixing plate and then went to find a brush and water. the paint dried while she searched. before her next painting she put the brush, water and plate together, then poured the paint.","amir took a blue coat from the hook because it looked like his. its owner came looking for it. amir checked the name inside and returned it. then he checked another blue coat and found his own name. ivy carried a seed packet to the bean bed because its picture looked like beans. the gardener showed her that it was a pea packet. ivy read the names on the remaining packets before taking the bean seeds.","amir took a blue coat from the hook because it looked like his. its owner came looking for it. amir checked the name inside and returned it. then he checked another blue coat and found his own name.","asha moved the meeting blanket from the tree to the porch when rain began. her friend kept waiting under the tree. asha went back and explained the change. her friend brought his bag to the dry porch. max changed the class shop’s opening time on his own note. the helpers arrived at the old time. before changing it again, he spoke to each helper and changed the shared sign. they arrived together.","asha moved the meeting blanket from the tree to the porch when rain began. her friend kept waiting under the tree. asha went back and explained the change. her friend brought his bag to the dry porch.","before_after","bela chose shiny thin paper for the base of her model because it looked special. the base bent under the model. she tried a plain stiff sheet, which held the model level, and used that sheet for the base. kofi chose a beautiful basket with very wide gaps to carry small counters. counters fell through. he tried a plain tub with solid sides. the counters stayed inside, so he carried them in the tub.","bela chose shiny thin paper for the base of her model because it looked special. the base bent under the model. she tried a plain stiff sheet, which held the model level, and used that sheet for the base.","bib","bo heard that a parcel belonged by the side door. he put it beside the playground door, but the collector waited elsewhere. bo asked which side door was meant, then moved it to the door beside the office. nia was asked to put the seed tray in a bright place. she chose the sunny outdoor wall, where the rain flooded it. she checked with the gardener and moved it to the bright indoor window the gardener had meant.","bo heard that a parcel belonged by the side door. he put it beside the playground door, but the collector waited elsewhere. bo asked which side door was meant, then moved it to the door beside the office.","book","ch","clap does not describe the pictured foreground action.","dependentClause","dig","distinguish_complete_dependent_clause_sentence","draw","eli tried to learn a long drum pattern all at once and kept losing his place. he practiced its first short part, then the next part. after joining the practiced parts, he could play the pattern through. rosa tried to copy a large map in one hurried drawing. several streets were missing. she copied one small square of the map at a time, checking each square before moving on. her new drawing included the streets.","eli tried to learn a long drum pattern all at once and kept losing his place. he practiced its first short part, then the next part. after joining the practiced parts, he could play the pattern through.","ellis checked one wheel on the model bus and said the bus was ready. a different wheel stuck when he pushed it. he turned every wheel by hand, freed the stuck one, and tried the bus again. anya pulled one handle on a carrying box to check it. when she lifted both handles, the unchecked handle came loose. after repairing it, she tested each handle separately before carrying the box.","ellis checked one wheel on the model bus and said the bus was ready. a different wheel stuck when he pushed it. he turned every wheel by hand, freed the stuck one, and tried the bus again.","every_except","finn glued a handle onto a cardboard basket and lifted it at once. the wet joint slid apart. he glued it again and left it flat until the joint was firm. this time the handle stayed on. aya packed a painted clay tile while its surface was still wet. the wrapping stuck to the picture. she painted a new tile and left it on the rack until it was dry before wrapping it.","finn glued a handle onto a cardboard basket and lifted it at once. the wet joint slid apart. he glued it again and left it flat until the joint was firm. this time the handle stayed on.","grace made a tiny book pocket for her partner without asking which book it would hold. the book was too wide. she asked to see the book and made a wider pocket that held it. dani set out a high stool for the visiting drummer without asking what she needed. the drummer’s feet could not reach her pedal. dani asked about the drum, then brought a low seat. the drummer could use the pedal.","grace made a tiny book pocket for her partner without asking which book it would hold. the book was too wide. she asked to see the book and made a wider pocket that held it.","hit","hop","hut","imani wrapped bright paper around every part of her toy cart. the paper jammed between a wheel and the frame. she cut the paper away from the moving wheel. the cart rolled again. felix tied a large bow across the mouth of his cardboard trumpet. almost no sound came out. he moved the bow onto the side, leaving the opening clear. he could hear the trumpet again.","imani wrapped bright paper around every part of her toy cart. the paper jammed between a wheel and the frame. she cut the paper away from the moving wheel. the cart rolled again.","j","jo kept the game scores in her head. after a break she could not remember which team had seven points. on the next game she marked every point on a scorecard. the teams could check the score after the break. mateo lent out the class puppets without writing down the borrowers. at tidy-up he did not know who still had one. next time he wrote each name beside a puppet picture and ticked it when the puppet returned.","jo kept the game scores in her head. after a break she could not remember which team had seven points. on the next game she marked every point on a scorecard. the teams could check the score after the break.","kai used a wide cup to pour beads into a narrow bottle. beads bounced onto the floor. he held a funnel in the neck and poured through it. the beads went into the bottle. lena used a thick brush to paint the tiny windows on her model. paint covered the wall around each window. she changed to a thin brush and painted the remaining windows without covering the walls.","kai used a wide cup to pour beads into a narrow bottle. beads bounced onto the floor. he held a funnel in the neck and poured through it. the beads went into the bottle.","kick","lap","let","luca piled beans above the rim of a small tray. they spilled whenever he moved it. he divided them between two trays, leaving space below each rim. he carried both trays without losing beans. esme stuffed every costume into one small bag. the zipper could not close. she moved some costumes into a second bag. both bags closed, and the costumes stayed inside on the walk to the hall.","luca piled beans above the rim of a small tray. they spilled whenever he moved it. he divided them between two trays, leaving space below each rim. he carried both trays without losing beans.","maya kept wiping water from under a plant pot. the puddle returned whenever she watered it because its tray was cracked. she replaced the tray. after the next watering, the shelf stayed dry. ben rebuilt the top of his block tower whenever it leaned. it kept leaning because a folded cloth was under one corner of the base. he flattened the cloth and rebuilt the base. the tower stayed upright.","maya kept wiping water from under a plant pot. the puddle returned whenever she watered it because its tray was cracked. she replaced the tray. after the next watering, the shelf stayed dry.","mira painted every paper flag before trying the new paint. when the flags dried, the paint cracked. she tried a little paint on spare paper, chose one that stayed smooth, and made the flags again. owen filled a whole watering can from an old jug. water leaked through a crack and soaked the bench. he poured a little water into the next jug first. that jug stayed dry underneath, so he used it.","mira painted every paper flag before trying the new paint. when the flags dried, the paint cracked. she tried a little paint on spare paper, chose one that stayed smooth, and made the flags again.","mock-foundation-word:drive","mock-foundation-word:ride","mock.v9.language.action.0.bake","mock.v9.language.action.0.bend","mock.v9.language.action.0.build","mock.v9.language.action.0.carry","mock.v9.language.action.0.chop","mock.v9.language.action.0.cook","mock.v9.language.action.0.drive","mock.v9.language.action.0.feed","mock.v9.language.action.0.lift","mock.v9.language.action.0.march","mock.v9.language.action.0.peel","mock.v9.language.action.0.pour","mock.v9.language.action.0.ride","mock.v9.language.action.0.smell","mock.v9.language.action.0.stand","mock.v9.language.action.0.stir","mock.v9.language.action.0.yawn","mock.v9.language.action.1.bake","mock.v9.language.action.1.bend","mock.v9.language.action.1.build","mock.v9.language.action.1.carry","mock.v9.language.action.1.chop","mock.v9.language.action.1.cook","mock.v9.language.action.1.drive","mock.v9.language.action.1.feed","mock.v9.language.action.1.lift","mock.v9.language.action.1.march","mock.v9.language.action.1.peel","mock.v9.language.action.1.pour","mock.v9.language.action.1.ride","mock.v9.language.action.1.smell","mock.v9.language.action.1.stand","mock.v9.language.action.1.stir","mock.v9.language.action.1.yawn","mock.v9.language.scope.baskets","mock.v9.language.scope.boxes","mock.v9.language.scope.brushes","mock.v9.language.scope.buttons","mock.v9.language.scope.candles","mock.v9.language.scope.claps","mock.v9.language.scope.colours","mock.v9.language.scope.crates","mock.v9.language.scope.dancers","mock.v9.language.scope.gate","mock.v9.language.scope.hats","mock.v9.language.scope.homework","mock.v9.language.scope.lanterns","mock.v9.language.scope.library","mock.v9.language.scope.lunch","mock.v9.language.scope.practice","mock.v9.language.scope.race","mock.v9.language.scope.rain","mock.v9.language.scope.red-blue","mock.v9.language.scope.seats","mock.v9.language.scope.seeds","mock.v9.language.scope.shelve