ed a complicated block pattern while her friend tried to remember every part. the copied pattern was different. olive drew a small plan with each block’s place. her friend used it to rebuild the pattern.","omar cut up his only pattern while trying a new shape. when the new shape failed, he could not return to the first pattern. for his next trial he traced a spare copy and cut that copy instead. cleo changed the only written plan for her puppet scene and later forgot the earlier ending. before her next change, she copied the plan onto another sheet. she could compare both endings and choose one.","omar cut up his only pattern while trying a new shape. when the new shape failed, he could not return to the first pattern. for his next trial he traced a spare copy and cut that copy instead.","only_not_sufficient","pain","pan","pen","pin","pipe","poppy compared two paper strips by holding one higher than the other. she chose the wrong longer strip. she laid them flat with their left ends together. now she could see which strip reached farther. yusuf counted how long two toy cars rolled, but started counting at different moments. his numbers did not compare the full journeys. he rolled them again and began counting at the start line each time.","poppy compared two paper strips by holding one higher than the other. she chose the wrong longer strip. she laid them flat with their left ends together. now she could see which strip reached farther.","quinn covered the whole card with a thick puddle of glue. it soaked through and wrinkled the paper. on the next card she used a thin line only where the pieces joined. the card stayed flat. hana kept adding soap to the wash bowl after the water was already bubbly. foam spilled over the edge. for the next bowl she added a small amount and stopped when it was enough to wash the tools.","quinn covered the whole card with a thick puddle of glue. it soaked through and wrinkled the paper. on the next card she used a thin line only where the pieces joined. the card stayed flat.","ravi spread his loose map pages on an outdoor bench. a gust blew two pages across the yard. he moved behind a closed window and spread them on an indoor table. the pages stayed where he put them. mila left her paper shop signs outside when rain began. the words ran down the paper. she made new signs and put them beneath the stall’s clear roof. rain fell around the stall, but the signs stayed dry.","ravi spread his loose map pages on an outdoor bench. a gust blew two pages across the yard. he moved behind a closed window and spread them on an indoor table. the pages stayed where he put them.","read","red","ren took every shelf out of a toy cupboard to clean it. later she could not tell which shelf had fitted each space. before cleaning the next cupboard, she put matching marks on the shelves and their spaces. they went back easily. theo pulled the ribbons out of a woven mat and forgot their order. before repairing another section, he drew where each ribbon went. he followed the drawing and put the ribbons back in the same places.","ren took every shelf out of a toy cupboard to clean it. later she could not tell which shelf had fitted each space. before cleaning the next cupboard, she put matching marks on the shelves and their spaces. they went back easily.","rob","rug","run","sal wrote that the picnic would begin at ten, but left out the day. his cousin arrived on the wrong morning. sal sent another note with both the day and the time, and his cousin came to the picnic. pia copied that the model needed three strips, but left out their length. her group cut strips too short for the roof. she checked the plan and wrote both the number and the length. the new strips reached across.","sal wrote that the picnic would begin at ten, but left out the day. his cousin arrived on the wrong morning. sal sent another note with both the day and the time, and his cousin came to the picnic.","sat","sip","sub","suri copied a striped flag and thought it was finished. when she held it beside the original, she noticed a missing white stripe. she added it, then compared the two flags once more. dan rebuilt a small bridge from a drawing and began putting the drawing away. he looked back at it and noticed a support he had left out. he added that support before trying the bridge.","suri copied a striped flag and thought it was finished. when she held it beside the original, she noticed a missing white stripe. she added it, then compared the two flags once more.","tape","tariq kept searching the same three drawers for a missing stamp. he could not remember which ones he had checked. he placed an empty card beside each searched drawer and moved to the next one. he found the stamp in a new drawer. mei looked for a book by jumping between several shelves. she kept returning to shelves she had already searched. she began at one end and checked each shelf in turn. on the next shelf she found the book.","tariq kept searching the same three drawers for a missing stamp. he could not remember which ones he had checked. he placed an empty card beside each searched drawer and moved to the next one. he found the stamp in a new drawer.","teeth","tess pushed all her seedlings into one corner of the tray. their leaves overlapped and bent. she moved them farther apart into the empty spaces. the leaves no longer pressed against one another. arun crowded the drying rack with wet paintings touching edge to edge. two pictures stuck together. he moved the next paintings onto separate spaces with gaps between them. they dried without sticking.","tess pushed all her seedlings into one corner of the tray. their leaves overlapped and bent. she moved them farther apart into the empty spaces. the leaves no longer pressed against one another.","type","until","wet","win","zara pushed the same puzzle piece harder each time it would not fit. the cardboard began to bend. she stopped pushing, turned the piece, and found the position that matched the gap. hugo pulled both ends of a knotted ribbon to free it. the knot grew tighter. he loosened one small loop with his fingers instead. the ribbon came free without another hard pull.","zara pushed the same puzzle piece harder each time it would not fit. the cardboard began to bend. she stopped pushing, turned the piece, and found the position that matched the gap.","ɪ","“Ask which seat lets a drummer reach the pedal.” explains episode 2, but episode 1 instead concerns this different action: Check the partner’s book before making its pocket. The choice leaves that episode unexplained.","“Check an old jug for leaks before filling it.” explains episode 2, but episode 1 instead concerns this different action: Test unfamiliar paint on a piece of spare paper. The choice leaves that episode unexplained.","“Check bookshelves one at a time from one end.” explains episode 2, but episode 1 instead concerns this different action: Mark drawers that have already been searched for a stamp. The choice leaves that episode unexplained.","“Check every bridge support against the supplied drawing.” explains episode 2, but episode 1 instead concerns this different action: Compare a copied flag with all its original stripes. The choice leaves that episode unexplained.","“Check every model bus wheel before calling it ready.” explains episode 1, but episode 2 instead concerns this different action: Test each carrying handle before lifting the box. The choice leaves that episode unexplained.","“Check the partner’s book before making its pocket.” explains episode 1, but episode 2 instead concerns this different action: Ask which seat lets a drummer reach the pedal. The choice leaves that episode unexplained.","“Check whether a bright growing place should be indoors.” explains episode 2, but episode 1 instead concerns this different action: Find out which door a collector actually means. The choice leaves that episode unexplained.","“Choose a counter container without gaps they can fa