lated_word/the-players-remained-inside-throughout-the-afternoon-be6e994737.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/the-players-went-outside-before-it-began-to-rain-87af3a2171.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/the-players-went-outside-while-the-rain-continued-26ca6e1436.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/the-repair-came-before-the-library-opened-ef49ba507b.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/the-song-had-already-ended-when-dad-put-out-the-candles-6123fb8f4d.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/the-waiting-children-beside-the-gate-d93a70e02b.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/tickets-first-went-on-sale-after-the-doors-opened-a81eecf00f.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/turn-a-model-opening-toward-the-person-watching-a7f92a9d1b.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/turn-a-puzzle-piece-rather-than-forcing-it-down-55416bd44f.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/until-the-heavy-garden-gate-finally-opened-for-all-of-us-5deba08daa.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/use-a-funnel-when-filling-a-narrow-bottle-e97299b4e5.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/use-a-handle-large-enough-for-your-hand-f8e95a2c82.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/use-a-straight-pole-to-display-the-finished-flag-1c952c634e.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/use-a-thin-brush-for-small-painted-details-08eedf08ce.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/use-a-thin-glue-line-where-the-card-pieces-join-4b65fce78c.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/use-sturdy-paper-for-a-list-that-stays-up-234f45d318.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/we-waited-until-the-gate-opened-efa91dc49a.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/while-i-held-the-ladder-dad-climbed-up-4191b1e681.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/while-i-held-the-tall-wooden-ladder-against-the-garden-wall-c14bb8181f.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/write-a-pattern-title-that-describes-its-finished-shape-19d6cf9361.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/isolated_word/write-the-owner-s-name-clearly-on-the-book-pocket-ba19b6d20e.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/read-5266f5f037.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/rob-d8f508738a.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/sob-6a7fb2b2b5.mp3","/audio/production/en-US/supplemental/tip-27fdea1a44.mp3","Ada hung the picture list above her own head. The younger children could not see what to collect. She crouched beside them, noticed the shelf in their way, and moved the list down where they could see it. Jin explained the model while holding its opening toward himself. His partner could not see the part he named. Jin moved around to his partner’s side and turned the model. The opening was now visible to both of them.","All the small crates were empty. Some large crates held books.","Alma poured paint onto a mixing plate and then went to find a brush and water. The paint dried while she searched. Before her next painting she put the brush, water and plate together, then poured the paint. Sam started building the puppet stage before checking its fasteners. He held two walls up for a long time while a friend searched for clips. Next time he collected the clips and walls together before joining the stage.","Amir took a blue coat from the hook because it looked like his. Its owner came looking for it. Amir checked the name inside and returned it. Then he checked another blue coat and found his own name. Ivy carried a seed packet to the bean bed because its picture looked like beans. The gardener showed her that it was a pea packet. Ivy read the names on the remaining packets before taking the bean seeds.","Asha moved the meeting blanket from the tree to the porch when rain began. Her friend kept waiting under the tree. Asha went back and explained the change. Her friend brought his bag to the dry porch. Max changed the class shop’s opening time on his own note. The helpers arrived at the old time. Before changing it again, he spoke to each helper and changed the shared sign. They arrived together.","Bela chose shiny thin paper for the base of her model because it looked special. The base bent under the model. She tried a plain stiff sheet, which held the model level, and used that sheet for the base. Kofi chose a beautiful basket with very wide gaps to carry small counters. Counters fell through. He tried a plain tub with solid sides. The counters stayed inside, so he carried them in the tub.","Bo heard that a parcel belonged by the side door. He put it beside the playground door, but the collector waited elsewhere. Bo asked which side door was meant, then moved it to the door beside the office. Nia was asked to put the seed tray in a bright place. She chose the sunny outdoor wall, where the rain flooded it. She checked with the gardener and moved it to the bright indoor window the gardener had meant.","Bo washed the brushes before putting them away.","Children could enter only after an adult opened the gate.","DRESS","Dad on the ladder beside the wall.","Dad put out the candles after the song ended.","Each child planted two seeds, and no child planted any more.","Eli tried to learn a long drum pattern all at once and kept losing his place. He practiced its first short part, then the next part. After joining the practiced parts, he could play the pattern through. Rosa tried to copy a large map in one hurried drawing. Several streets were missing. She copied one small square of the map at a time, checking each square before moving on. Her new drawing included the streets.","Ellis checked one wheel on the model bus and said the bus was ready. A different wheel stuck when he pushed it. He turned every wheel by hand, freed the stuck one, and tried the bus again. Anya pulled one handle on a carrying box to check it. When she lifted both handles, the unchecked handle came loose. After repairing it, she tested each handle separately before carrying the box.","Every basket contained apples, but only one basket also contained pears.","Every seat beside the window was taken. Two seats beside the door were free.","Every ticket had been sold before the doors opened.","Every tray except the green one held two cups. The green tray was empty.","Everyone in the show was either a dancer or a singer. Every dancer wore a blue ribbon. No singer wore a blue ribbon.","Finn glued a handle onto a cardboard basket and lifted it at once. The wet joint slid apart. He glued it again and left it flat until the joint was firm. This time the handle stayed on. Aya packed a painted clay tile while its surface was still wet. The wrapping stuck to the picture. She painted a new tile and left it on the rack until it was dry before wrapping it.","Grace made a tiny book pocket for her partner without asking which book it would hold. The book was too wide. She asked to see the book and made a wider pocket that held it. Dani set out a high stool for the visiting drummer without asking what she needed. The drummer’s feet could not reach her pedal. Dani asked about the drum, then brought a low seat. The drummer could use the pedal.","Imani wrapped bright paper around every part of her toy cart. The paper jammed between a wheel and the frame. She cut the paper away from the moving wheel. The cart rolled again. Felix tied a large bow across the mouth of his cardboard trumpet. Almost no sound came out. He moved the bow onto the side, leaving the opening clear. He could hear the trumpet again.","Jin fed the rabbit after lunch but before the music lesson.","Jo kept the game scores in her head. After a break she could not remember which team had seven points. On the next game she marked every point on a scorecard. The teams could check the score after the break. Mateo lent out the class puppets without writing down the borrowers. At tidy-up he did not know who still had one. Next time he wrote each name beside a puppet picture and ticked it when the puppet returned.","KIT","Kai used a wide cup to pour beads into a narrow bottle. Beads bounced onto the floor. He held a funnel in the neck and poured through it. The beads went into the bottle. Lena used a thick brush to paint the tiny windows on her model. Paint covered the wall around each window. She changed to a thin brush and painted the remaining windows without covering the walls.","LOT","Lena used all the round buttons and none of the square buttons.","Luca piled beans above the rim of a small tray. They spilled whenever he moved it. He divided them between two trays, leaving space below each rim. He carried both trays without losing beans. Esme stuffed every costume into one small bag. The zipper could not close. She moved some costumes into a second bag. Both bags closed, and the costumes stayed inside on the walk to the hall.","Maya kept wiping water from under a plant pot. The puddle returned whenever she watered it because its tray was cracked. She replaced the tray. After the next watering, the shelf stayed dry. Ben rebuilt the top of his block tower whenever it leaned. It kept leaning because a folded cloth was under one corner of the base. He flattened the cloth and rebuilt the base. The tower stayed upright.","Mina painted every flag except the yellow flag. She left that flag plain.","Mira painted every paper flag before trying the new paint. When the flags dried, the paint cracked. She tried a little paint on spare paper, chose one that stayed smooth, and made the flags again. Owen filled a whole watering can from an old jug. Water leaked through a crack and soaked the bench. He poured a little water into the next jug first. That jug stayed dry underneath, so he used it.","Neither the red bag nor the blue bag held a towel. Each towel was in the basket.","No books were put on the top shelf. Every new book went on the bottom shelf.","Noor tied the ribbon tightly around an empty gift box. Then she had to undo it to put the gift inside. For the next gift she packed and closed the box before tying its ribbon. Leo mixed a batch of plaster before making a space for the mold. While he searched for a clear tray, the mixture became too stiff to pour. For the next batch he set out the mold and tray before mixing.","Not every child finished the puzzle. Three children were still working.","Olive described a complicated block pattern while her friend tried to remember every part. The copied pattern was different. Olive drew a small plan with each block’s place. Her friend used it to rebuild the pattern. Dev called out the drum rhythm once and expected the group to remember it. They stopped at different places. He drew a row of beat marks and pointed along them. The group could follow the same rhythm.","Omar cut up his only pattern while trying a new shape. When the new shape failed, he could not return to the first pattern. For his next trial he traced a spare copy and cut that copy instead. Cleo changed the only written plan for her puppet scene and later forgot the earlier ending. Before her next change, she copied the plan onto another sheet. She could compare both endings and choose one.","Only boxes with a star were sent to the hall. Some starred boxes stayed behind.","Only children wearing hats could join the walk. Amir wore a hat and joined.","Only pupils who returned a signed form could take a book home. Not all those pupils chose a book.","Poppy compared two paper strips by holding one higher than the other. She chose the wrong longer strip. She laid them flat with their left ends together. Now she could see which strip reached farther. Yusuf counted how long two toy cars rolled, but started counting at different moments. His numbers did not compare the full journeys. He rolled them again and began counting at the start line each time.","Quinn covered the whole card with a thick puddle of glue. It soaked through and wrinkled the paper. On the next card she used a thin line only where the pieces joined. The card stayed flat. Hana kept adding soap to the wash bowl after the water was already bubbly. Foam spilled over the edge. For the next bowl she added a small amount and stopped when it was enough to wash the tools.","Ravi spread his loose map pages on an outdoor bench. A gust blew two pages across the yard. He moved behind a closed window and spread them on an indoor table. The pages stayed where he put them. Mila left her paper shop signs outside when rain began. The words ran down the paper. She made new signs and put them beneath the stall’s clear roof. Rain fell around the stall, but the signs stayed dry.","Ren took every shelf out of a toy cupboard to clean it. Later she could not tell which shelf had fitted each space. Before cleaning the next cupboard, she put matching marks on the shelves and their spaces. They went back easily. Theo pulled the ribbons out of a woven mat and forgot their order. Before repairing another section, he drew where each ribbon went. He followed the drawing and put the ribbons back in the same places.","STRUT","Sal wrote that the picnic would begin at ten, but left out the day. His cousin arrived on the wrong morning. Sal sent another note with both the day and the time, and his cousin came to the picnic. Pia copied that the model needed three strips, but left out their length. Her group cut strips too short for the roof. She checked the plan and wrote both the number and the length. The new strips reached across.","Suri copied a striped flag and thought it was finished. When she held it beside the original, she noticed a missing white stripe. She added it, then compared the two flags once more. Dan rebuilt a small bridge from a drawing and began putting the drawing away. He looked back at it and noticed a support he had left out. He added that support before trying the bridge.","Tariq kept searching the same three drawers for a missing stamp. He could not remember which ones he had checked. He placed an empty card beside each searched drawer and moved to the next one. He found the stamp in a new drawer. Mei looked for a book by jumping between several shelves. She kept returning to shelves she had already searched. She began at one end and checked each shelf in turn. On the next shelf she found the book.","Tess finished before Noor, and Noor finished before Sol.","Tess pushed all her seedlings into one corner of the tray. Their leaves overlapped and bent. She moved them farther apart into the empty spaces. The leaves no longer pressed against one another. Arun crowded the drying rack with wet paintings touching edge to edge. Two pictures stuck together. He moved the next paintings onto separate spaces with gaps between them. They dried without sticking.","The class stood up before the last clap. They sat down after it.","The library remained closed until the worker fixed the door. It opened as soon as the repair was finished.","The players stayed inside unless the rain stopped. The rain continued all afternoon.","The waiting children beside the gate.","There were two tables of lanterns. No lantern on the left table was lit. All the lanterns on the right table were lit.","Until the heavy garden gate finally opened for all of us.","Until the soil dried, Rosa did not water the pot. She watered it as soon as it was dry.","While I held the tall wooden ladder against the garden wall.","Zara pushed the same puzzle piece harder each time it would not fit. The cardboard began to bend. She stopped pushing, turned the piece, and found the position that matched the gap. Hugo pulled both ends of a knotted ribbon to free it. The knot grew tighter. He loosened one small loop with his fingers instead. The ribbon came free without another hard pull.","crawl does not describe the pictured foreground action.","drink does not describe the pictured foreground action.","ee changes the required spelling of the exact dictated word.","foot","goat","mock-foundation-word:bake","mock-foundation-word:cook","mock.v9.boundary-comprehension.listening.ask-about-the-need.b5",