","nap","neither the red bag nor the blue bag held a towel. each towel was in the basket.","neither","no books were put on the top shelf. every new book went on the bottom shelf.","not every child finished the puzzle. three children were still working.","not_all","only boxes with a star were sent to the hall. some starred boxes stayed behind.","only children wearing hats could join the walk. amir wore a hat and joined.","only pupils who returned a signed form could take a book home. not all those pupils chose a book.","only_after","only_necessary","our team arrived the game began","play","print","rail","read-picture-word:bin","read-picture-word:cab","read-picture-word:cap","read-picture-word:cob","read-picture-word:cub","read-picture-word:fin","read-picture-word:fog","read-picture-word:nut","read-picture-word:van","read-picture-word:web","read-picture-word:wig","read-picture-word:yak","room","sea","spoon","ss","temporal_scope","tess finished before noor, and noor finished before sol.","the class stood up before the last clap. they sat down after it.","the doorbell rang we opened the door","the glue had dried our model was ready","the kettle boiled dad made tea","the library remained closed until the worker fixed the door. it opened as soon as the repair was finished.","the light turned green the cars moved forward","the players stayed inside unless the rain stopped. the rain continued all afternoon.","the wind grew stronger we brought the washing inside","there were two tables of lanterns. no lantern on the left table was lit. all the lanterns on the right table were lit.","tin changes at least one recorded phoneme.","tree","tʃ","unless","until the soil dried, rosa did not water the pot. she watered it as soon as it was dry.","vat","vet","ways","write does not describe the pictured foreground action.","writing_revision","yam","yes","æ","ɔɪ","ɔː","“Check that a block base is firm and level.” does not explain this correction. The spoken block description was hard to retain and a drawn plan supplied a continuing reference; stability and fair shares were not the copying problem.","“Check that the pages show the whole walking route.” does not explain this correction. The wind scattered loose pages, and moving indoors sheltered them; map size and route coverage would not stop the gust.","“Choose a blanket large enough for the visitors.” does not explain this correction. The friend waited at the old place because the move had not been explained; blanket size and carrying food would not tell the friend where to go.","“Choose a box that is easy to carry.” does not explain this correction. The parcel reached the wrong door because the direction was unclear; box size and keeping a path clear would not identify the intended door.","“Choose a bus color that passengers can recognize.” does not explain this correction. An unchecked wheel stuck after one different wheel had passed a check; bus color and seat space would not test the other wheels.","“Choose a map large enough for the group to share.” does not explain this correction. The wind scattered loose pages, and moving indoors sheltered them; map size and route coverage would not stop the gust.","“Choose a picnic place with room for everyone.” does not explain this correction. The note left out the day, causing an arrival on the wrong morning; an envelope or larger picnic site would not supply the missing day.","“Choose a puzzle with enough pieces for everyone.” does not explain this correction. Pushing bent the puzzle piece, while turning it revealed the fit; sorting colors or sharing pieces would not change the failing method.","“Choose card colors that stand out against the wall.” does not explain this correction. Excess glue soaked and wrinkled the card; the card colors and the storage tray would not reduce that excess.","“Choose clear pictures of the objects to collect.” does not explain this correction. The younger children could not see past the shelf; strong paper and clear pictures would not move the list into their view.","“Choose colors that make a toy cart easy to find.” does not explain this correction. Wrapping jammed a moving wheel; attractive colors and a comfortable handle would not clear the wheel.","“Choose colors that make the model’s shape easy to see.” does not explain this correction. The attractive thin base bent under the load; visible colors and display measurements would not make that base stiff enough.","“Choose fabric that will move freely in the wind.” does not explain this correction. Comparison revealed a missing stripe after Suri thought she had finished; fabric movement and the display pole would not reveal that omission.","“Choose flag colors that visitors can see clearly.” does not explain this correction. The flag paint cracked because it had not been tried on spare paper; separating colors or making flags visible would not test that paint.","“Choose paint colors that show against the background.” does not explain this correction. The paint dried while Alma searched for tools; color contrast and protecting a finished picture would not have put the tools ready beforehand.","“Choose plant labels that can survive getting wet.” does not explain this correction. The seedlings pressed against one another because they were crowded; labels and counting would not leave room between the leaves.","“Choose plants that fit the space on a shelf.” does not explain this correction. The same puddle returned because the tray was cracked; plant size and dividing watering jobs would not repair the leak.","“Choose scissors suited to the thickness of the paper.” does not explain this correction. Cutting the only pattern removed the earlier version; suitable scissors and a title would not preserve an uncut copy.","“Choose scissors that can cut the paper strips cleanly.” does not explain this correction. Holding the strips at different starting positions gave a misleading comparison; cutting tools and storage would not align their ends.","“Choose strong paper for a pocket that holds books.” does not explain this correction. The pocket was too narrow for the actual book; strong paper and an owner name would not establish the required size.","“Choose teams with equal numbers of players.” does not explain this correction. Jo forgot the score after a break and used written marks to retain it; team size and practice time would not preserve the score.","“Choose wrapping that is large enough for the box.” does not explain this correction. The empty box had been tied before the gift was inside, so the ribbon had to be undone; wrapping size and gift choice would not correct that order.","“Count the seedlings before carrying a full tray.” does not explain this correction. The seedlings pressed against one another because they were crowded; labels and counting would not leave room between the leaves.","“Give both teams a chance to practice first.” does not explain this correction. Jo forgot the score after a break and used written marks to retain it; team size and practice time would not preserve the score.","“Give each builder a share of the available blocks.” does not explain this correction. The spoken block description was hard to retain and a drawn plan supplied a continuing reference; stability and fair shares were not the copying problem.","“Give every player a chance to lead the music.” does not explain this correction. Eli lost his place in a long pattern and succeeded after practicing its short parts; choosing an instrument or sharing leadership was not the difficulty.","“Give the cart a handle that is comfortable to hold.” does not explain this correction. Wrapping jammed a moving wheel; attractive colors and a comfortable handle would not clear the wheel.","“Hang a wet coat where it can dry.” does not explain this correction. A similar appearance led Amir to take another coat; drying coats or lowering hooks would not identify the owner.","“Keep a finished painting safe from dusty shelves.” does not explain this correction. The paint dried while Alma searched for tools; color contrast and protecting a finished picture would not have put the tools ready beforehand.","“Keep a list of people who borrow the stamp set.” does not explain this correction. Tariq repeated searches because he had not tracked the checked drawers; dry storage and a borrower list would not organize this search.","“Keep a note of who has borrowed each tray.” does not explain this correction. Beans spilled because the small tray was overfilled; sorting beans and recording tray loans would not provide more space.","“Keep a record of how many beads you collect.” does not explain this correction. The wide cup could not direct beads into the narrow neck; sorting or counting beads would not change that opening.","“Keep cleaning cloths away from the toy collection.” does not explain this correction. Ren could not restore the shelves to their places and solved this with matching marks; choosing cupboard contents or moving cloths would not record the arrangement.","“Keep coats low enough for children to reach.” does not explain this correction. A similar appearance led Amir to take another coat; drying coats or lowering hooks would not identify the owner.","“Keep cut paper strips together until the craft begins.” does not explain this correction. Holding the strips at different starting positions gave a misleading comparison; cutting tools and storage would not align their ends.","“Keep different paint colors in their own pots.” does not explain this correction. The flag paint cracked because it had not been tried on spare paper; separating colors or making flags visible would not test that paint.","“Keep loose card pieces in a labelled storage tray.” does not explain this correction. Excess glue soaked and wrinkled the card; the card colors and the storage tray would not reduce that excess.","“Keep the path beside a busy door clear.” does not explain this correction. The parcel reached the wrong door because the direction was unclear; box size and keeping a path clear would not identify the intended door.","“Leave enough space inside a bus for its seats.” does not explain this correction. An unchecked wheel stuck after one different wheel had passed a check; bus color and seat space would not test the other wheels.","“Listen to other players before choosing an instrument.” does not explain this correction. Eli lost his place in a long pattern and succeeded after practicing its short parts; choosing an instrument or sharing leadership was not the difficulty.","“Match a gift to the interests of its owner.” does not explain this correction. The empty box had been tied before the gift was inside, so the ribbon had to be undone; wrapping size and gift choice would not correct that order.","“Measure a cupboard before choosing what to store.” does not explain this correction. Ren could not restore the shelves to their places and solved this with matching marks; choosing cupboard contents or moving cloths would not record the arrangement.","“Measure the model before deciding where to display it.” does not explain this correction. The attractive thin base bent under the load; visible colors and display measurements would not make that base stiff enough.","“Plan what a basket will hold before decorating.” does not explain this correction. The wet glued joint slid apart because Finn lifted it too soon; handle size and planning the contents would not make that joint firm.","“Send a picnic invitation in a strong envelope.” does not explain this correction. The note left out the day, causing an arrival on the wrong morning; an envelope or larger picnic site would not supply the missing day.","“Share the watering jobs between the gardeners.” does not explain this correction. The same puddle returned because the tray was cracked; plant size and dividing watering jobs would not repair the leak.","“Sort differently colored beads into separate groups.” does not explain this correction. The wide cup could not direct beads into the narrow neck; sorting or counting beads would not change that opening.","“Sort puzzle pieces into groups with similar colors.” does not explain this correction. Pushing bent the puzzle piece, while turning it revealed the fit; sorting colors or sharing pieces would not change the failing method.","“Sort the beans by size before comparing them.” does not explain this correction. Beans spilled because the small tray was overfilled; sorting beans and recording tray loans would not provide more space.","“Store stamps where damp air cannot reach them.” does not explain this correction. Tariq repeated searches because he had not tracked the checked drawers; dry storage and a borrower list would not organize this search.","“Take a bag that keeps picnic food together.” does not explain this correction. The friend waited at the old place because the move had not been explained; blanket size and carrying food would not tell the friend where to go.","“Use a handle large enough for your hand.” does not explain this correction. The wet glued joint slid apart because Finn lifted it too soon; handle size and planning the contents would not make that joint firm.","“Use a straight pole to display the finished flag.” does not explain this correction. Comparison revealed a missing stripe after Suri thought she had finished; fabric movement and the display pole would not reveal that omission.","“Use sturdy paper for a list that stays up.” does not explain this correction. The younger children could not see past the shelf; strong paper and clear pictures would not move the list into their view.","“Write a pattern title that describes its finished shape.” does not explain this correction. Cutting the only pattern removed the earlier version; suitable scissors and a title would not preserve an uncut copy.","“Write the owner’s name clearly on the book pocket.” does not explain this correction. The pocket was too narrow for the actual book; strong paper and an owner name would not establish the required size.",32,40,42,43,64,65,67,68,72,77,81,"A tiny root appeared we drew it in our notebook","A tiny root appeared we. Drew it in our notebook.","A. Tiny root appeared we drew it in our notebook.","Blending the three recorded phonemes in order makes big.","Blending the three recorded phonemes in order makes fed.","Blending the three recorded phonemes in order makes hip.","Blending the three recorded phonemes in order makes hot.","Blending the three recorded phonemes in order makes jug.","Blending the three recorded phonemes in order makes lab.","Blending the three recorded phonemes in order makes lot.","Blending the three recorded phonemes in order makes mud.","Blending the three recorded phonemes in order makes mug.","Blending the three recorded phonemes in order makes mum.","Blending the three recorded phonemes in order makes rot.","Blending the three recorded phonemes in order makes sap.","Blending the three recorded phonemes in order makes sob.","Blending the three recorded phonemes in order makes ten.","Blending the three recorded phonemes in order makes tin.","Blending the three recorded phonemes in order makes tip.","Dad climbed up","My shoes were wet i left them by the door","My shoes were wet i. Left them by the door.","My. Shoes were wet i left them by the door.","Our team arrived the game began","Our team arrived the. Game began.","Our. Team arrived the game began.","The doorbell rang we opened the door","The doorbell rang we. Opened the door.","The glue had dried our model was ready","The glue had dried our. Model was ready.","The kettle boiled dad made tea","The kettle boiled dad. Made tea.","The key preserves the passage''s after relationship.","The key preserves the passage''s all only one relationship.","The key preserves the passage''s all some relationship.","The key preserves the passage''s before relationship.","The key preserves the passage''s every exception relationship.","The